141 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (Exchange rate volatility is one of the important factors influencing international trade and economic performance. Changes in currency values affect the prices of exported products, production costs, business profits and international competitiveness.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (This project examines the asymmetric impact of exchange rate volatility on export performance. Asymmetric impact means that positive and negative exchange rate movements may influence exports differently.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (For example, currency depreciation may make domestic products cheaper for foreign buyers and increase export demand. However, depreciation may also increase the cost of imported raw materials and machinery. Similarly, currency appreciation may reduce export price competitiveness but lower the cost of imported production inputs.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The main objective of this study is to understand how exchange rate fluctuations affect export performance and why their effects differ across countries and economic conditions.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The project uses secondary information collected from research papers, academic journals, economic reports and international publications.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
146 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The main reference study examines selected G7, Asian and West African countries. It uses economic indicators and the Panel Autoregressive Distributed Lag \(ARDL\) approach to investigate the relationship between exchange rate volatility and export competitiveness.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
147 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The study considers variables such as real effective exchange rates, exchange rate volatility, terms of trade, trade openness, export price index, inflation and interest rates.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The findings indicate that exchange rate volatility has an important influence on exports. Its effects differ across economic regions because of differences in financial systems, trade policies and economic structures.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
